"How far apart the two eyes sit. 1.00 would be physically correct in the portal, but the world behind it is greatly reduced and reads as flat — 1.50 gives it depth. The 3D window works at a different scale and is far more sensitive: there the near field decides, and a little is a lot. No effect in the 2D window." = "How far apart the two eyes sit. 1.00 would be physically correct in the portal, but the world behind it is greatly reduced and reads as flat — 1.50 gives it depth. The 3D window works at a different scale and is far more sensitive: there the near field decides, and a little is a lot. No effect in the 2D window.";
"3D window only: the distance at which both images coincide. Nearer things step out of the screen, further ones lie behind it. Set too far forward the background becomes unpleasant; too far back, the foreground. About 1000 is the character's distance from the camera." = "3D window only: the distance at which both images coincide. Nearer things step out of the screen, further ones lie behind it. Set too far forward the background becomes unpleasant; too far back, the foreground. About 1000 is the character's distance from the camera.";
"Smooths polygon edges. Takes effect at once. No function in the simulator — Metal rejects the depth resolve there." = "Smooths polygon edges. Takes effect at once. No function in the simulator — Metal rejects the depth resolve there.";
"Renders into a correspondingly larger texture and averages it down. The most effective lever against ragged edges, because it also works inside textures and at the window's own edge. The cost rises with the square — at 2.00 therefore fourfold." = "Renders into a correspondingly larger texture and averages it down. The most effective lever against ragged edges, because it also works inside textures and at the window's own edge. The cost rises with the square — at 2.00 therefore fourfold.";
"The compositor's render resolution would be the strongest lever, but it cannot be raised here: any value above the platform's own stops the layer from starting." = "The compositor's render resolution would be the strongest lever, but it cannot be raised here: any value above the platform's own stops the layer from starting.";
"Both VR modes. The readouts keep the arrangement the game gives them — the pane they are laid onto simply grows, which pushes the corners apart in both directions at once. Takes effect at once." = "Both VR modes. The readouts keep the arrangement the game gives them — the pane they are laid onto simply grows, which pushes the corners apart in both directions at once. Takes effect at once.";

